WEBVTT

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:13.200
Romeo's Blue Skies

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:13.200
"To the Sky..."

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:17.840
<i>Overlooking the rows of houses and stores</i>

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:22.250
<i>from the highest vantage,</i>

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:27.360
<i>Such things as tears and sadness</i>

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:31.500
<i>will quickly vanish</i>

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:37.060
<i>The birds, wind, and sunshine...</i>

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:41.250
<i>...all are your friends</i>

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:46.320
<i>I'll carry this dream farther than far</i>

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:51.410
<i>...no matter the distance...</i>

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:58.170
<i>I long to fly freely</i>

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:02.450
<i>through the blue sky in my heart...</i>

00:01:02.490 --> 00:01:05.380
<i>The far distant blue sky</i>

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:12.830
<i>It flows into tomorrow</i>

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:25.260
Takara Fansubs

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:32.450
The Black Brothers

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:32.450
<i>Long ago, many children in the world lived in such destitution</i>

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:36.550
<i>that it is hard for us to imagine today.</i>

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:42.950
<i>However, bravery and friendship filled their hearts.</i>

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:46.960
<i>And yes... Romeo's heart as well...</i>

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:52.250
Episode 1:

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:52.250
In the Alps: The Crisis of a Small Village

00:01:56.160 --> 00:02:03.160
<i>Our story begins in a small Swiss village near the Italian border.</i>

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:17.160
Mmm... All right... I'm up...

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:26.160
Hey, Piccolo!

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:31.060
Oh shoot!!!

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:36.760
Good morning!

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:40.960
You sleepyhead!
You're not gone yet?

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:41.960
I can still make it!

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:44.060
Romeo! Your father's lunch!

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:47.870
I'm off!

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:53.770
Piccolo... it's a race against the sunrise!

00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:00.070
To the right - the shortcut!

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:03.870
Here goes, Piccolo!

00:03:12.570 --> 00:03:13.770
Good morning!

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:15.770
Uh-oh!

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:26.470
Pardon me! I'm in a hurry!

00:03:39.370 --> 00:03:40.570
Made it...

00:04:14.570 --> 00:04:17.170
<i>Today's going to be great.
I just know it will.</i>

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:22.100
<i>At the town festival -- today's the day I become a hero!</i>

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:29.440
Thank you for the hard work each morning.

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:30.880
Here's this week's portion.

00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:33.080
Ah, Dad'll be so pleased!

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:35.580
It's been a tough year...

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:38.980
I wish I could give you more...

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:41.980
No, no...
Thank you very much, Father.

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:47.580
Oh yeah! Father -- they're having the "Hero's Tree Climb"

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:50.380
at this year's festival, aren't they?

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:54.880
Of course. We would never skip such a thing in this village.

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:58.220
I wonder who will win this year...

00:04:59.390 --> 00:05:01.390
Oh, nothing, sorry...

00:05:01.390 --> 00:05:02.390
I knew it!

00:05:04.090 --> 00:05:04.990
Anita.

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:08.240
You're planning on entering the Hero's Tree Climb, aren't you?

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:09.090
I'm right, right?

00:05:09.190 --> 00:05:10.390
Is that true, Romeo?

00:05:10.390 --> 00:05:11.490
Ummm...

00:05:11.690 --> 00:05:15.490
Well don't! If you do something dangerous like that I'll never forgive you!

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:17.690
I've already decided!

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:18.690
Goodbye!

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:21.390
Wait! Romeo!

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:23.800
How could you! And I'm so worried about you!

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:27.010
Eh? Romeo in the tree-climb?

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:30.400
Yup! He said he's going to win the championship!

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:34.900
And he says he'll get cornbread after he wins.

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:37.400
He says he's gonna let you taste the bread,

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:39.200
made from real corn for the first time in a long time!

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:40.400
He was bragging...

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:42.900
Bread? Wow!

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:46.900
That sleepyhead is unbelieveable.

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:49.190
His grown-up talk, it's his only mature thing...

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:53.610
And I'm always telling him too...

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:57.310
Even if we don't have bread...
so long as everyone's fine...

00:05:57.610 --> 00:05:58.660
Mom!

00:05:59.110 --> 00:06:01.310
I'm going to do the Hero's Tree Climb too!

00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:02.310
Me too!!

00:06:02.310 --> 00:06:03.310
Absolutely not!

00:06:03.310 --> 00:06:05.610
That would be the end of it, if you two got hurt.

00:06:06.610 --> 00:06:07.610
Mom...

00:06:07.710 --> 00:06:10.510
Even bigger boys than Romeo are doing the tree-climb.

00:06:10.910 --> 00:06:13.010
It's quite dangerous enough for Romeo.

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:15.320
Dad got the championship, didn't he?

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:18.420
He says he's gonna become just like Dad, he did!

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:23.120
Jessica...

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:25.720
Isn't it just like him?

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:28.620
He really is Roberto's boy...

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:31.820
Yes! He's Romeo's hero after all!

00:06:32.420 --> 00:06:35.020
Romeo will listen to his dad, for sure.

00:06:35.420 --> 00:06:38.820
He'll tell him what to do, I'm sure.

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:45.420
Say Romeo...

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:47.720
Do you like me?

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:50.730
So you hate me?

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:52.730
I didn't say I hate you!

00:06:53.330 --> 00:06:55.030
Then kiss me!

00:06:57.630 --> 00:06:59.130
If you like me, kiss me.

00:07:08.530 --> 00:07:09.730
Jeez, that's it!

00:07:09.730 --> 00:07:12.030
But it was so funny!

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:15.830
You dope.
You never listen to what I say.

00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:17.730
That's not true.

00:07:17.730 --> 00:07:19.530
Then don't do such dangerous things!

00:07:20.030 --> 00:07:23.230
You can't become a hero by getting scared off.

00:07:23.640 --> 00:07:27.500
Dad got the championship -- at just 14.

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:30.040
You're only 10, aren't you, Romeo?

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:31.440
I'm already 11!

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:55.640
It's terrible!

00:07:56.140 --> 00:07:57.740
How long is this going to last?

00:07:57.740 --> 00:08:00.240
Not a drop of rain for 5 months!

00:08:04.140 --> 00:08:07.340
The way things are going, the town's crops are being wiped out.

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:10.940
Probably it's going to get harder and harder for everyone.

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:12.740
What can we do?

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:14.240
Nothing to do but wait for the rain.

00:08:14.950 --> 00:08:15.930
Not likely!

00:08:22.050 --> 00:08:26.150
Sorry. And it's you who's suffering the most, too.

00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:28.950
It was your family's potatoes and peaches

00:08:28.950 --> 00:08:31.650
that were ruined by that damn badger

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:34.550
that came at the beginning of summer... I'm sorry, Roberto.

00:08:35.050 --> 00:08:37.750
There's still corn left here.

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:40.750
I'm praying for your last field, here...

00:08:41.050 --> 00:08:44.360
that rain falls first of all, right here.

00:08:54.750 --> 00:08:57.450
Uh... Dad... In today's festival...

00:08:58.450 --> 00:08:59.450
I mean...

00:09:00.260 --> 00:09:00.860
Romeo!

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:07.160
F... F... fire! Fire!

00:09:12.060 --> 00:09:13.360
Watch out!

00:09:13.660 --> 00:09:15.260
There are dried shrubs all over!

00:09:15.260 --> 00:09:18.260
A fire would cause an inferno in a wink of an eye!

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:21.660
Sorry...

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:41.060
Romeo.

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:42.460
Yes?

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:45.260
The Hero's Tree Climb, you wanted to enter it...

00:09:46.760 --> 00:09:47.860
If you want to still...

00:09:48.970 --> 00:09:50.770
I'm saying it's okay.

00:09:52.470 --> 00:09:54.470
But in exchange, watch yourself please.

00:09:54.810 --> 00:09:59.020
A true hero is someone who doesn't worry his mom.

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:01.870
Dad!

00:10:04.840 --> 00:10:06.120
Thanks a lot, Dad!

00:10:15.870 --> 00:10:18.270
Crap! The wind would come on the day of the festival...

00:11:01.070 --> 00:11:04.670
It's him! The God of Death!

00:11:15.170 --> 00:11:16.470
The God of Death!?

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:22.470
He goes from town to town buying kids from poor families in financial trouble.

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:24.080
Buying kids?

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:25.860
What does he do then?

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:27.880
Brings them to the city and sells them.

00:11:28.380 --> 00:11:30.680
They are forced to work until they die,

00:11:32.480 --> 00:11:33.680
That bastard...

00:11:33.930 --> 00:11:37.080
looking for kids to take to his slaughterhouse.

00:12:02.980 --> 00:12:03.980
Wait here a bit.

00:12:03.980 --> 00:12:04.480
Ok.

00:12:06.980 --> 00:12:09.880
Hey Piccolo, I'm really good at tree-climbing, you know...

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:12.880
Maybe not as good as you Piccolo...

00:12:13.290 --> 00:12:15.320
But no way I'd lose to any of the other kids!

00:12:16.090 --> 00:12:18.330
I can't wait to do it!

00:12:22.790 --> 00:12:23.990
Hey, Roberto...

00:12:23.990 --> 00:12:24.590
Hi.

00:12:26.190 --> 00:12:27.090
Mr. Scara...

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:28.990
I know, Roberto.

00:12:28.990 --> 00:12:31.790
I can tell by your face that you can't pay the bill yet.

00:12:32.290 --> 00:12:33.090
Sorry...

00:12:33.390 --> 00:12:36.360
Next week I'll at least try to pay off the sugar bill or something.

00:12:36.490 --> 00:12:38.290
Yes, I sure hope so.

00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:41.800
In the meantime, no flour or butter.

00:12:41.800 --> 00:12:44.900
Now, Scara! You could at least help him a little...

00:12:44.900 --> 00:12:47.400
Times are tough because of this drought...

00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:50.440
and you know very well that Roberto and his family have been

00:12:50.450 --> 00:12:53.240
the ones most hurt by it.

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:55.700
I find it very unfortunate,

00:12:55.800 --> 00:12:56.700
but a bill is a bill.

00:12:57.100 --> 00:12:59.200
You guys bills are piling up a lot too.

00:12:59.200 --> 00:13:01.300
You will be able to pay, won't you?

00:13:02.310 --> 00:13:03.210
Yes.

00:13:03.710 --> 00:13:05.310
Sorry, Roberto.

00:13:05.310 --> 00:13:07.310
It's okay. Thanks, though.

00:13:08.110 --> 00:13:10.510
Anyway, I'll bring something next week.

00:13:10.710 --> 00:13:11.670
Right.

00:13:12.510 --> 00:13:12.910
Bye.

00:13:19.710 --> 00:13:20.510
That guy is...

00:13:20.510 --> 00:13:21.410
I know.

00:13:24.510 --> 00:13:27.610
The God of Death.
That's what he's called.

00:13:30.610 --> 00:13:32.650
That's your kid out front, right?

00:13:34.190 --> 00:13:36.660
How about it? Feel like selling the boy?

00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:42.830
Do so, and your bill will be paid

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:44.520
and you'll get plenty of pocket change.

00:13:48.320 --> 00:13:49.720
Sell me the boy.

00:13:50.520 --> 00:13:51.520
Damned monster!

00:13:52.820 --> 00:13:53.920
What a slimeball!

00:13:53.920 --> 00:13:55.650
Roberto, ignore him.

00:13:59.820 --> 00:14:00.620
I'll tell you this about Roberto...

00:14:00.620 --> 00:14:02.120
he's not one to sell his kid

00:14:02.120 --> 00:14:03.640
no matter how tough the times are.

00:14:03.830 --> 00:14:05.930
He still has one field, anyway.

00:14:05.930 --> 00:14:06.930
That's right.

00:14:06.930 --> 00:14:09.650
Roberto wouldn't be shaken up by something like this.

00:14:10.730 --> 00:14:11.530
I see.

00:14:13.530 --> 00:14:14.830
I'll remember that.

00:14:20.530 --> 00:14:21.130
Dad!

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:25.830
The Hero's Tree Climb is finally coming up!

00:14:26.030 --> 00:14:28.390
It doesn't matter if you lose just do your best.

00:14:29.330 --> 00:14:32.230
I'm not going to lose.
I'm your kid, after all.

00:14:34.530 --> 00:14:35.730
That's true, isn't it Romeo?

00:14:35.740 --> 00:14:37.220
Dad!

00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:41.840
Hey hey!

00:14:41.840 --> 00:14:43.940
You've gotta win, big brother!

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:45.640
You've gotta!

00:14:46.040 --> 00:14:49.640
Of course! I'll get you lots of bread to eat tomorrow!

00:14:49.640 --> 00:14:51.640
We've heard that story.

00:14:51.940 --> 00:14:55.240
Really! All your grown-up talk, it's your only grown-up thing.

00:14:55.240 --> 00:14:57.440
Huh? You think so?

00:15:01.740 --> 00:15:05.640
Unfortunately, I hate happy little families...

00:15:12.240 --> 00:15:13.440
<i>I'll tell you this about Roberto...</i>

00:15:13.450 --> 00:15:16.710
<i>he's not one to sell his kid, no matter how though the times are.</i>

00:15:16.950 --> 00:15:18.850
He still has one field, anyway.

00:15:29.150 --> 00:15:31.750
Burn! Down to the last shred of hope!

00:15:39.950 --> 00:15:44.660
Ok everyone! Just for today only,
let's forget the drought and bad harvest.

00:15:44.950 --> 00:15:47.250
Just raise a ruckus from the bottom of your belly!

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:51.150
Yeah! Let's surprise God so that he sends us rain!

00:15:51.150 --> 00:15:52.650
Atta girl, Grandma!

00:15:57.450 --> 00:15:59.350
I still think you shouldn't.

00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:02.050
If I can lift this much, then I could win.

00:16:05.850 --> 00:16:07.050
I knew it - you'd better quit now.

00:16:08.060 --> 00:16:09.260
Here goes...

00:16:11.660 --> 00:16:12.960
Pipsqueak!

00:16:14.460 --> 00:16:16.560
Heard you're gonna enter the Hero's Tree Climb.

00:16:16.660 --> 00:16:17.760
Give it up!

00:16:18.660 --> 00:16:20.490
Unless I try, I'll never know.

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:24.960
Anita, wait til you see how I thrash Romeo for you today.

00:16:25.360 --> 00:16:27.560
Romeo's absolutely going to win.

00:16:28.060 --> 00:16:30.960
Then I'm gonna become Romeo's wife!

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:33.260
Really?

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:34.260
That's right.

00:16:34.370 --> 00:16:35.870
A-Anita!

00:16:37.970 --> 00:16:39.670
He's gonna steal Anita from you!

00:16:39.670 --> 00:16:41.470
Better not lose, Embellino!

00:16:47.270 --> 00:16:48.370
Ok, that's enough!

00:16:49.170 --> 00:16:50.470
Let's go, stand it up!

00:16:51.370 --> 00:16:52.070
There!

00:16:53.170 --> 00:16:54.480
It's the owl!

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:56.370
The Hero's Tree Climb is about to start!

00:16:57.970 --> 00:17:01.870
I thought it wouldn't work out this year but 
it looks like it'll be a good fight after all.

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:02.470
Yeah.

00:17:05.980 --> 00:17:08.080
Romeo received some truly good parents.

00:17:10.480 --> 00:17:11.780
Yes, father.

00:17:14.780 --> 00:17:16.280
Time passes so quickly...

00:17:16.490 --> 00:17:18.630
It's been 10 years since that day...

00:17:20.280 --> 00:17:21.480
Say, Jessica...

00:17:21.480 --> 00:17:23.280
have you kept that day a secret from...

00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:24.980
I mean...

00:17:25.880 --> 00:17:28.400
have you kept it a secret about his parents?

00:17:35.080 --> 00:17:35.880
I understand.

00:17:35.880 --> 00:17:37.980
In due course that time will come.

00:17:58.690 --> 00:18:01.290
All right everyone, I know you've been waiting for it!

00:18:01.290 --> 00:18:02.690
It's time for the Hero's Tree Climb!

00:18:06.890 --> 00:18:08.590
This year we have 4 climbers.

00:18:08.990 --> 00:18:10.890
First, Marco!

00:18:12.190 --> 00:18:14.490
Mannio Piccalio!

00:18:14.890 --> 00:18:15.890
Embellino!

00:18:16.190 --> 00:18:18.890
And... Romeo!

00:18:22.090 --> 00:18:26.640
As everyone knows, the one who brings down
the owl statue from the top of the pole

00:18:26.680 --> 00:18:31.090
will be named the "True Hero"!

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:33.890
Hurray! Go for it!

00:18:34.100 --> 00:18:35.710
Romeo! Good luck!

00:18:35.900 --> 00:18:37.800
Huh? That little runt is entering?

00:18:38.700 --> 00:18:41.500
Runt or no runt! That kid has great spirit!

00:18:41.500 --> 00:18:43.800
'Cause he's my grandkid!

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:45.700
All right, I know...

00:18:46.500 --> 00:18:49.730
Obviously Romeo's the one who will get the owl!

00:18:49.900 --> 00:18:51.800
All right! Time to start the match!

00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:08.700
All right brother! Go for it!

00:19:08.700 --> 00:19:10.400
Don't lose, Romeo!

00:19:10.400 --> 00:19:13.400
Embellino! Let Romeo have it!

00:19:13.710 --> 00:19:14.810
Mr. Scara!

00:19:17.710 --> 00:19:21.110
Romeo! If you lose, don't bother coming home!

00:19:22.710 --> 00:19:23.310
Leggo!

00:19:23.610 --> 00:19:25.210
Lemme go or you're gonna get it!

00:19:25.210 --> 00:19:26.610
Sure - as soon as you pry off my cold, dead hands!

00:19:26.610 --> 00:19:27.810
C'mon -- leggo!

00:19:27.910 --> 00:19:29.810
That's it! You and me are through!

00:19:35.510 --> 00:19:37.810
A one-on-one! You two do your best!

00:19:40.710 --> 00:19:42.110
Go! Go!

00:19:42.110 --> 00:19:44.210
Romeo, don't you lose!

00:19:45.420 --> 00:19:47.920
Romeo! Just a bit more!

00:19:49.520 --> 00:19:51.320
Bring down the owl!

00:20:14.320 --> 00:20:16.220
Romeo's the only one left!

00:20:34.720 --> 00:20:37.420
Fire!

00:20:40.420 --> 00:20:42.720
Fire!

00:20:51.520 --> 00:20:52.520
It's...

00:20:54.120 --> 00:20:55.320
The hill!

00:20:55.320 --> 00:20:56.620
The hill's burning!

00:21:02.820 --> 00:21:06.320
Romeo's... Romeo's family's cornfield is burning!

00:21:53.820 --> 00:21:57.520
<i>Dad told me that I was just a selfish baby.</i>

00:21:58.230 --> 00:21:59.230
<i>I'm not a baby.</i>

00:21:59.790 --> 00:22:00.640
<i>Dad just...</i>

00:22:00.830 --> 00:22:03.230
<i>Dad just doesn't understand at all!</i>

00:22:04.290 --> 00:22:09.720
See you then!

00:22:04.290 --> 00:22:09.720
<i>Destiny's Beginnings:
The Family Within the Flames</i>

00:22:04.290 --> 00:22:09.720
Next time:

00:22:11.680 --> 00:22:15.510
<i>"Si Si Ciao ~ On These Roman Roofs"</i>

00:22:24.300 --> 00:22:28.400
<i>Si Si Ciao, why do the good times</i>

00:22:28.500 --> 00:22:32.700
<i>seem to end so soon?</i>

00:22:32.900 --> 00:22:36.900
<i>Si Si Ciao, we're all friends</i>

00:22:37.100 --> 00:22:41.100
<i>Let's meet again on these Roman roofs</i>

00:22:41.710 --> 00:22:46.010
<i>Your laughing voice dances</i>

00:22:46.010 --> 00:22:49.910
<i>Once again in the sky</i>

00:22:50.310 --> 00:22:57.210
<i>Your pocket bursting with memories</i>

00:22:58.910 --> 00:23:02.810
<i>Si Si Ciao, goodbye but for now</i>

00:23:03.010 --> 00:23:07.010
<i>Let's meet again on these Roman roofs</i>
